2. Recover lost migration state: inspect `git reflog`, `git log --oneline --all`, `git stash list`, and `git diff <baseline>...HEAD`. Identify migration changes that were reverted (build files, security config, javax→jakarta, Jackson, properties, Dockerfile/CI). Report what was reverted and whether it must be restored.
3. Inventory: modules, build files, resolved dependency tree, profiles and all config files (application*.yml/properties, bootstrap, external config), Dockerfile, Jenkinsfile/CI, start scripts, the UI boundary.
4. Build and test the current state and record the exact failures and warnings as the baseline.

